{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgn558aWH2PvUA6oqhadG", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "As far as I can tell, no one has been told. The nightly run crashed before it could alert anyone, and I didn't send anything myself.\n\n- **The nightly run:** the crash happened at `os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir)` in `pipeline/review.py`. That line runs before the findings are written and before `notify.send` is called, so no alert was queued.\n- **This machine:** there's no `spool/` directory, no `NOTIFY_SPOOL` set, and nothing under `/srv`. The only spool writes I triggered were in the unit tests, which use temp directories.\n\nI can't see the runner's spool or the relay's delivery logs from here. To confirm, someone with access to the runner should check that `spool/outgoing` is empty, or that no `[spend sev3]` messages were delivered on the night of 2026-11-04.\n\nThe $412.30 overspend is recorded only in `data/runlog/2026-11-04.jsonl`, and the finance on-call hasn't been notified. A rerun would send the alerts for the first time, which is the intended behaviour. Check with the finance on-call before you rerun."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "4928ca61-30c9-4934-9b43-df0cdcc2677d", "uuid": "0b50e03c-1a90-4d4e-8c93-61a91444b549", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T17:30:04.104Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgn558HtcCma4rr8rTfdS"}
